BEHAVIOR bytes-to-string

DESCRIPTION
  Produces a `string` (length-prefixed, self-describing) from the first len
  bytes of src, using the caller-owned buffer buf as its backing store. The
  composition half: string-pack writes [len][content] into buf, then SET makes
  the string output point at buf. SOUND ONLY while buf outlives the returned
  string (the caller owns buf, e.g. pattern MEMORY) -- exactly the collections
  lifetime model. buf needs len+8 bytes.

CONTRACT
  INPUT src bytes 65536
  INPUT len int 8
  INPUT buf bytes 65544
  OUTPUT str string
  REQUIRES string-pack@4bb1e8d7
  GUARANTEES writes_output

HASH 8b5b6eaf

COMPOSITION
  CALL string-pack src len buf
  SET str buf
END
